  "judge": {
    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "correctness",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "Removes on.pull_request.paths, so the workflow runs on every PR and the required `test` check always reports. A first step (`id: changes`) gets the PR's changed files from the GitHub API and writes site=true/false to GITHUB_OUTPUT. The build/test step is gated with `if: steps.changes.outputs.site == 'true'`. On a docs-only PR the detect step passes and the gated step is skipped, so the job still ends in success. Good details: the token is passed via env, it paginates, it avoids a grep -q SIGPIPE race under pipefail, and it sets least-privilege permissions. Small deductions: the change is unverified beyond YAML parsing, which the agent says openly. The job also depends on the API call working: if `gh` hits a transient error, the job fails instead of passing. A checkout plus `git diff` would have been a sturdier way to detect changes."
      },
      {
        "name": "restraint",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "Only workflows/ci.yml changed. The added permissions block is needed for the API-based detection, and the comment explains the required-check constraint, so both relate to the task. The agent did not touch README.md, did not move the workflow out of the nonstandard workflows/ directory (it flagged this instead), and did not add a concurrency group or a third-party action. No unrelated edits."
      }
    ],
    "overall": 9.0
  },
